    "angle_domain_caveat": "Reader cold_trig uses 64 angles (i+1)/257, approximately 0.00389 to 0.24903 rad. Runtime reach phi is 1.2*(age+.78), hence 0.936 to 1.536 rad for legal 0 to 500 ms ages, with different rational denominators. The 21.27x result is a real local cold-kernel measurement for the declared 64 angles, not a measured workload representative of runtime source ages. Exact polynomial identity covers the supported domain, but its end-to-end/cold-miss speedup there remains unmeasured.",
